From: MGS2 RG353VS compatibility port
Subject: [PATCH 85] dmsynth: make sink startup, loss recovery and clocks coherent

The production sink has four connected lifetime failures:

* both worker threads signal "started" even when setup failed, so Activate
  returns S_OK and latches active=TRUE for a sink with no live worker;
* a runtime DSERR_BUFFERLOST makes the render thread return before releasing
  its samples, buffer and synth, while active remains TRUE forever;
* written and the resume marker survive a deactivate/activate even though
  activate_time is replaced, producing an incoherent sample/reference map;
* patch 83 rebases before the underrun cursor correction, and its 64-bit
  activate_time is read unlocked on 32-bit ARM.

Propagate exact startup status through the existing events, close worker
handles and reset stop events on every path, keep the render thread alive with
a bounded 250 ms retry while DirectSound reports BUFFERLOST, and release every
reference on all exits. Reset the render-owned cursor at activation, resync it
before a resume rebase, and take the existing sink lock around activate_time.
No normal-path polling or hot-thread log is added.

